 for DSM-IV axis I disorders</article-title><source>Patient edition (SCID-I/P, version 2.0, 4/97 revision)</source><year>1997</year><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>New York State Psychiatric Institute</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="b15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gavish</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Weizman</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Karp</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Decreased peripheral benzodiazepine sites in platelets of neuroleptic treated schizophrenics</article-title><source>Eur J Pharmacol</source><year>1986</year><volume>121</volume><fpage>275</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2870930</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goodwin</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoven</surname><given-names>CW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bipolar-panic comorbidity in the general population: prevalence and associated morbidity</article-title><source>J Affect Dis</source><year>2002</year><volume>55</volume><fpage>51</fpage><lpage>4</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hu</surname><given-names>ZY</given-names></name><name><surname>Jung-Testas</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Robel</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Neurosteroids: steroidogenesis in primary cultures of rat glial cells after release of aminoglutethimide blockade</article-title><source>Biochem Biophys Res Commun</source><year>1989</year><volume>161</volume><fpage>917</fpage><lpage>22</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2735928</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b18"><citation citation-type="journal">